target/
tmp/
.sota

# Not a build directory: FHIR's own `target` property (SearchParameter/
# StructureDefinition reference constraints) gets a source module named
# `target/`, same as any other property. The unanchored `target/` rule above
# would otherwise silently exclude real, hand-documented source from every
# clone and from `cargo publish`'s dirty-tree check — found doing exactly
# that, publishing the `fhir` crate.
!fhir/src/r5/parse/all/target/

# CycloneDX SBOMs (O10.10). Generated per release by `cargo cyclonedx` and
# uploaded as a CI artifact, not committed: an SBOM describes one build, and a
# stale one in the tree is worse than none — the same failure the map assets
# had before F-40 gave them a regeneration path.
*.cdx.json
